  "solution": "The logic that follows here is shown below:\n\n**(2ⁿd number - 1st number)² = 3rd number **\n\n**(2, 8, 36) **\n\n⇒(8 - 2)²=36\n\n⇒6²=36\n\n⇒36=36\n\n**(4, 9, 25)**\n\n⇒(9 - 4)²=25\n\n⇒5²=25\n\n⇒25=25\n\nBy, checking the options\n\n1. (14, 18, 9)\n\n⇒(18 - 14)² = 9\n\n⇒4² = 9\n\n⇒16 ≠ 9\n\n**2. (13, 20, 49)**\n\n**⇒(20 - 13)² = 49**\n\n**⇒7² = 49**\n\n**⇒49 = 49**\n\n3. (21, 15, 35)\n\n⇒(15 - 21)² = 35\n\n⇒(-6)² = 35\n\n⇒36 ≠ 35\n\n4. (12, 14, 26)\n\n⇒(14 - 12)² = 26\n\n⇒2² = 26\n\n⇒4 ≠ 26\n\nHence, the correct answer is __**option 2**__.",
